md = f"# Scanner accuracy inside the fit decision\n\nThe runnable change is a signed-clearance contact port and a scanner/scanbody acquisition choice from independent published measurements. It refuses actual fit certification from RMS, group medians, or a color-map maximum. No 10× gain or physical gap validation is established.\n\n| Frozen construction | Actual result | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1: 40 µm + global scanner summary | Max retrospective clinical summary error {r1['max_error_um']:.1f} µm; {r1['wrong_group_summary_accepts']} wrong group-summary acceptance; 28/28 transferred implant bounds fail | Global-to-gap universal shortcut fails; software/version and estimand transfer UNKNOWN |\n| R2: choose commercial scanner + scanbody | Prime/SB2: position median44.89 µm vs Prime/SB1:82.14 µm; {r2['primary_geometry_reduction_fraction'] * 100:.2f}% reduction | Retrospective measured geometry improvement against a specified scanner-only reference; not prospective validation |\n| R2 composed medians, 40 µm process + 4mm lever | {r2['scanner_only_baseline']['screens'][2]['composed_median_gap_screen_um']:.2f} → {r2['selected']['screens'][2]['composed_median_gap_screen_um']:.2f} µm; selected lever flip {r2['selected']['lever_flip_mm']:.2f}mm | Engineering screen changes across120; actual gap law remains UNKNOWN; 2/28 median-as-span bounds fail |\n| R3 count model | Source column C46/PB sums6 for nominal5 scans; stopped before contact experiment | Failed gate retained unchanged |\n| R4 registration + signed contact | At least {r4['forced_sign_switches_lower']}/{r4['eligible_ending_scan_tooth_observations']} eligible ending-side scan/tooth max-area signs must change PB→FB; {r4['unknown_pair_observations']}/80 nominal observations UNKNOWN | Same-image single-bin convention required; one6-count and one4-count column quarantined, no renormalization |\n| R4 same modeled axial error size ±57.5 µm | Projected margin40 vs {r4['case_bounds']['same_rms_contraction']['gap_upper_um'][0]:.2f} µm; bridge near margin also{r4['bridge_near_margin_um']:.2f} µm | Own analytic fixture; direction/contact determine the answer |\n| Strong equal-information controls | Scalar arithmetic, exhaustive acquisition and signed interval vertices TIE; largest contact discrepancy {r4['max_control_error_um']:.2e} µm | No method novelty established |\n\nPrimary clinical reference: Boeddinghaus et al., DOI10.1007/s00784-015-1430-7, local primary abstract Results: Omnicam149µm and CaraTRIOS112µm **medians**, with IQRs114–218 and94–149. They are not individual safety bounds or current software benchmarks. Clinical2020 i500/CS3600 values are secondary transcriptions in local PMC10923227 Table1, clearly marked. They are not used to fit the model.\n\nThe external implant data are DOI10.1371/journal.pone.0295790 Tables5/8/11; the external signed regional data are DOI10.1186/s12903-023-03101-z Tables2–5. These source quantities can refute our shortcuts. The cone/ring fixtures are explicitly our own geometry, not external facit. The suggested DOI10.1016/j.prosdent.2025.01.007 is a systematic review of marginal-gap measurement methods and is not a paired per-scanner calibration dataset.\n\nThe strict120µm criterion is the requested engineering marginal-gap example. It is not asserted as an implant passive-fit clinical limit. R4's marginal observable is a **projected vertical margin-plane separation**, rather than absolute marginal discrepancy or full Euclidean closest-edge gap. Moving to the native anatomical SDF consumer requires that observable mapping and independently measured fields.\n\nAll failed gates, original PREREGs, source table counts, open<-450µm tails and frozen predictions remain. Actual K42 certificate: ABSTAIN_UNKNOWN. No source/native graph, shared cell, other checkout, or dataset was changed.\n"
