readme = f"# Scanner → signed field → fit decision\n\n**Idea.** A scanner's global error does not say whether an intaglio wall is too large or too small. A small inward error can stop insertion and lift a whole bridge. The demo combines published configuration measurements with a signed, datum-labelled contact operation.\n\nRun from this directory:\n```sh\n./run_all.sh\n```\nThe command uses only existing local measurement data,1 thread, no GPU, and creates a timestamped `replays/` bundle. Archived PREREGs/predictions/results stay intact. Dependencies are the existing Python3/NumPy/SciPy installation plus system Matplotlib (the plotting subprocess disables incompatible user-site NumPy). Expected peak memory is below1GB; no heavy scheduler required. Copy the small package plus its source files to reproduce elsewhere; see SOURCE_MANIFEST.json for exact input paths and hashes.\n\n![Results](FIGURE.png)\n\n| Result | Value | Evidence |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Scanner-only model's largest retrospective clinical summary error | {r1['max_error_um']:.1f}µm | [Primary clinical abstract](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25693497/); cross-year aliases unresolved |\n| Selected Prime/SB2 vs specified Prime/SB1 reference |44.89 vs82.14µm position medians; −{r2['primary_geometry_reduction_fraction'] * 100:.1f}% | [Primary implant measurements](https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0295790), Table5 |\n| Composed-median budget with40µm nominal term and4mm lever |150.76→96.06µm | Separate measured medians, Table5/8; not a gap quantile |\n| Registration changes observed ending-side sign |at least64/70 eligible;10/80 UNKNOWN | [Primary regional measurements](https://doi.org/10.1186/s12903-023-03101-z), Tables3/5, single-bin convention |\n| Same modeled axial magnitude, different sign |40 vs374.38µm projected gap | Own cone fixture at3° half taper; controls agree to1e-8µm |\n| Actual physical fit certificate |UNKNOWN | Paired scanner/process/contact-gap data missing |\n\n**What does not hold.** This is not a calibrated physical crown predictor, a scanner purchase recommendation, or a10× result. Scalar mean/RMS, marginal medians, and regional color maxima cannot certify a whole contact surface. The published scanner study and clinical gap studies differ in geometry, versions and estimands. Clinical2020 i500/CS3600 numeric rows are visibly marked secondary-table transcriptions. Two source columns have bin sums6 and4 for nominal5 scans; neither was repaired. Open tails are unbounded. All equally informed conventional controls tie.\n\n**What a lab can try.** `exports/` holds a closed mm die and two cone-ring calibration witnesses, not clinical restorations. `MEASUREMENT_REQUEST.json` asks for independently referenced whole-wall signed clearance, the manufacturing/margin bound, and a shared insertion datum. Predictions were frozen before any new measurement. Under the declared3° model, the nominal axial error flips the120µm decision at−44.19µm. A single measured point suffices only if the rest of the wall is already bounded; that prerequisite is currently UNKNOWN. Measure the same specimens' projected vertical marginal gap and the full3D closest-edge gap separately. Use `code/signed_gap.py` only with the stated port contract.\n\n**Data and licenses.** Only existing local numerical literature tables/primary abstract metadata were used; no mesh/image/raw dataset was downloaded and no patient-level data were extracted. PMC10729975 (PLOS One), PMC10265779 (BMC Oral Health), PMC10048864 (IJERPH) are CC BY4.0 per their embedded licenses. PMC10923227 is CC BY-NC-SA4.0; the extracted clinical2020 facts retain that source and its primary DOI. Exact embedded statements are in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json. The primary clinical abstract is used for numerical facts; its full publisher text is not redistributed. Fixture geometry and code are new local research artifacts. Teeth3DS, ToothFairy2, Bits2Bites, MMDental and mandibular-defect datasets are **not used** in this demo.\n"
(ROOT / 'README_DEMO.md').write_text(readme)
